the us government has released a secret  intelligence report that finds the saudi  crown prince responsible for approving  the murder  of the journalist jamal khashoggi mr  khashoggi disappeared in 2018  after entering the saudi consulate in  istanbul  where he is believed to have been killed  and dismembered  our defense and security correspondent  aleister bunkel joins me now from  washington uh alistair no big surprise  but nonetheless still very significant  this report  yeah i think you're right i mean i don't  think there's anything much in the  report that we didn't already  know but what it does is it puts on  public record  the cia in particular their assessment  that it was mohammed bin salman  who was behind the community of killian  jamal khashoggi  back in 2018 he was the one who  authorized  the action of the team that went to  istanbul and  ultimately killed the saudi journalist  the report  makes that clear in no uncertain terms  but it does outline  some of the reasons why the cia have  come to that assessment and just one of  them i'll read out  uh says that the team included seven  members of mohammed bin salman's elite  personal protective detail  known as the rapid intervention force  the rapid intervention force  exists to defend the crown prince  answers only to him  and had directly participated in earlier  dissident suppression operations in the  kingdom at saudi arabia  and abroad at the crown prince's  direction so it's pretty unequivocal  in that respect as i say it doesn't  really  tell us anything that most people didn't  expect anyway but it does signal  you know really quite a a sizable shift  in approach to saudi arabia from the  united states  under president biden for many years  through many presidencies  um saudi arabia has been a key middle  east ally for  important strategic and security reasons  including it should be said during the  obama administration president obama uh  mohammed bin salman  donald trump was very cozy with the  the saudi administration uh during his  tenure but  president biden has made it very clear  he's going to take a very different  approach  he will speak only to king salman not  muhammad bin salman he is described  before saudi arabia  as a prior state he has stopped  funding arms sales for saudi arabia  because of their use in yemen  and now he must decide having published  this report  what kind of action he is going to take  against the crown prince and what effect  that might have  on diplomatic relations
 

